  "notes": "USAGE:\nA literary and intellectual term used to describe deep, sustained thinking, particularly about philosophical or abstract subjects. More elevated in register than ordinary {考|かんが}える.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {思索|しさく}にふける (to be absorbed in thought)\n- {思索|しさく}を{重|かさ}ねる (to think deeply over time)\n- {思索|しさく}を{巡|めぐ}らす (to turn thoughts over in one's mind)\n- {思索|しさく}{的|てき} (contemplative, meditative)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {熟考|じゅっこう}: careful deliberation (more practical, decision-oriented)\n- {瞑想|めいそう}: meditation (spiritual or physical practice)\n- {考察|こうさつ}: examination, analysis (more academic)",
